1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:01,273
OK.

2
00:00:01,273 --> 00:00:02,086
So...

3
00:00:02,086 --> 00:00:05,208
I want to start by saying I appreciate the rigor here.

4
00:00:05,208 --> 00:00:09,748
The framework you're describing is one I've come across
before and it's well-grounded work.

5
00:00:09,748 --> 00:00:14,485
But I do want to push back a little, because I'm not
sure it's the right starting point for us.

6
00:00:15,685 --> 00:00:20,747
A lot of what I'm reading in your draft is grounded
in research with general adult populations.

7
00:00:20,747 --> 00:00:23,567
And that work matters, I'm not dismissing it.

8
00:00:23,567 --> 00:00:26,517
But most of our participants don't fit those samples.

9
00:00:26,633 --> 00:00:31,334
We've had community health educators working with
these specific communities for years now, and they've

10
00:00:31,334 --> 00:00:34,981
built up a lot of knowledge about what actually shifts
behavior here.

11
00:00:34,981 --> 00:00:40,192
What worries me is that if your recommendations are
mostly built from the outside literature, we'll end

12
00:00:40,192 --> 00:00:44,674
up with something that's intellectually sound but
doesn't reflect what our team already knows works

13
00:00:44,674 --> 00:00:45,499
on the ground.

14
00:00:46,699 --> 00:00:49,950
I don't want you to walk away thinking we're starting
from scratch.

15
00:00:49,950 --> 00:00:51,506
That's not what I'm asking.

16
00:00:51,506 --> 00:00:56,219
What I'd like to see is how you're going to weigh
what our educators have told you against what the

17
00:00:56,219 --> 00:00:57,438
literature says.

18
00:00:57,438 --> 00:01:02,024
And honestly, if you haven't talked to them yet, I'd
like to know what your plan is there.

